SUMMARY:Michael Jefry Stevens & Friends | The “Bon Voyage” Concert!
DESCRIPTION:A special farewell evening celebrating pianist and composer Michael Jefry Stevens before his move back north. Stevens reunites with longtime collaborator Michael Rabinowitz—whose work together began in New York City’s legendary Mosaic Sextet\, alongside Dave Douglas\, Mark Feldman\, Joe Fonda\, and Harvey Sorgen. Their acclaimed recordings and adventurous improvisations have earned international recognition in the jazz world. \nJoined by acclaimed bassist Steve LaSpina and drummer Rick Dilling\, this quartet brings together masterful musicianship\, creative interplay\, and deep jazz tradition for one unforgettable night of modern jazz\, improvisation\, and celebration — don’t miss this final WNC performance. \n$10 weekdays -$15 weekends at the door (all ticket proceeds are 100% passed to the band\, backed by a living wage guarantee from Hotel Eve) \n*Reserve a table in advance\, or join us impromptu the night of the show. Reservations/advance tickets are recommended for preferred seating\, but not required. Tickets are available at the door on a first-come\, first-served basis.  Event Details and Tickets \nHotel Eve is your locally rooted\, speakeasy jazz club & cocktail bar\, hidden in the heart of Downtown Asheville. Mysteriously not a hotel…check in for spirits\, souls and jazz! We’re tucked away\, on purpose. You’ll find us behind the gate nestled between Virtue Boutique and Dane Wells Gallery at 56 N Lexington Avenue in downtown Asheville. Step through\, take a left into the courtyard\, check in for Spirits\, Souls & Jazz. We’ll be waiting on the other side. hotelevejazz.com \n 
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/michael-jefry-stevens-friends-the-bon-voyage-concert/
LOCATION:Hotel Eve Jazz\, 56 N Lexington Avenue\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
